+## Mutation negative controls and before/after evidence
+
+`tests/mutation-v2.test.mjs` now contains **8 focused tests**, all observed passing in `node --test tests/mutation-v2.test.mjs` after the harness fix. Canonical test command receipts and complete TAP output are retained by the overall review gate. A passing negative-control test means the harness correctly refused successful mutation coverage, not that the deliberately broken mutant was killed.
+
+| Control | Exact intervention | Required/observed classification and evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Empty inventory | Call `auditMutants([])` | Throws `ZERO_MUTANTS`; cannot produce a passing zero-denominator report. |
+| Unapplied mutation | Required source text does not exist | `NOT_APPLIED`, applied=false, KILLED=0, passed=false. |
+| No-op mutation | Replacement is identical to original | `NOT_APPLIED`, applied=false, KILLED=0, passed=false; separate from unapplied text in the same test. |
+| Host crash | Inject `process.exit(7)` immediately inside verifyV2 | Actual process `CRASH`; classification `CRASHED`, KILLED=0, passed=false. |
+| Invalid host output | Inject `return null` inside verifyV2 | `INVALID_OUTPUT`, KILLED=0, passed=false; no malformed report becomes a semantic witness. |
+| Broken positive | Change final positive projection to well-formed CONTRADICTED/BROKEN_POSITIVE_CONTROL | Positive process still COMPLETED, positive_preserved=false; `CONTROL_BROKEN`, KILLED=0, passed=false. |
+| Inner checker crash | Bridge exits 7 only when the corpus contains poison; G24 positive remains normal, G12 is the witness | Host witness report is valid/COMPLETED with product CANNOT_RECOMPUTE; recursive execution evidence detects failed native checker. `CRASHED`, checker_execution_failed=true, KILLED=0, positive preserved. |
+| Invalid inner native output with exit 0 | Bridge emits literal JSON null and exits 0 only on poison; G24 positive remains normal | Host witness report remains valid/COMPLETED, exit 0, product CANNOT_RECOMPUTE. `INVALID_OUTPUT`, checker_output_invalid=true, checker_execution_failed=false, KILLED=0, positive preserved. |
+| Legitimate native semantic refusal | Direct classifier control with TRUSTLESS_NATIVE_NOT_VALID / semanticVerdict NOT_VALID | Not classified as malformed output. Native NOT_VALID is a valid negative vocabulary item; existing adapter tests independently exercise native refusal behavior. This classifier test is not counted as an executed semantic mutant. |
+
+During this review, the inner-null control exposed a real harness defect: the original harness counted a well-formed host CANNOT_RECOMPUTE result as KILLED merely because it differed from baseline CONTRADICTED. `reports/v0.2/mutation-invalid-native-before.json` records an actual fresh pre-fix probe, exact UTC start/end, source and input SHA-256 identities, full reproduction source, G24/G12 IDs and the false successful kill receipt. This was recorded before changing the harness, not reconstructed afterward.
+
+The correction is confined to the mutation harness. It rejects known checker transport/output failure codes and non-semantic CANNOT_RECOMPUTE/REJECTED_MALFORMED outcomes, while preserving actual nested crashes as CRASHED and native NOT_VALID as semantic. The focused post-fix inner-null control records INVALID_OUTPUT and zero kills through executable assertions. A malformed-output testing contract would need a separately explicit fault model; this semantic catalog has none.
+
+A separate product finding is covered by G29/M13: native authenticated opaque scanner assertions previously satisfied LOCAL_RECOMPUTATION policy. `reports/v0.2/grade-finding-before.json` truthfully retains the actual earlier stdout and explicitly identifies absent full input/report files, source snapshot hash and timestamp. The product guard and `tests/trustless-grade-v2.test.mjs` preserve the native AUTHENTICATED_REPORT result but require product INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE. Wrapper replay must not upgrade scanner execution grade.
+
+
+A **HIGH composition finding** is covered by G30/M14. The pre-fix core replaced the top-level guarantee status with its transfer status, so a correctly reproduced native PRF VIOLATED result with a PRESERVED transfer was presented as overall VERIFIED. Correct transfer of a negative conclusion preserves that negative conclusion; it does not certify a positive relation. The same composition path also weakened unsupported, malformed and unavailable checker outcomes into mere insufficiency.
+
+`reports/v0.2/prf-composition-finding-before.json` retains actual read-only pre-fix probes with full inputs/reports, UTC times, runtime, source SHA-256 values, input digests and explicitly recorded fault injection. Its reproduced-negative-preserved case records native VIOLATED / amount_mismatch, native replay REPRODUCED, transfer PRESERVED and the incorrect overall VERIFIED. G30's oracle is a fresh independently selected literal 50-versus-100 mismatch, not an expected answer generated from the projection. The fixed projection separately validates and consumes guarantee.productProjection without erasing PRESERVED transfer; G30 requires overall CONTRADICTED while G15 still permits VERIFIED. M14 removes only this product projection consumption and is killed by the changed semantic result with G15 preserved.
+
+G30 adds a distinct composition witness to G16's changed-dependency transfer failure and G21's UNVERIFIABLE native relation. It remains one bounded supplied award/settlement tuple. It proves neither real settlement provenance, completeness of the caller's accepted basis, nor a semantic link between that tuple and the surrounding positive RVR artifact predicate. The surrounding RVR result intentionally remains VERIFIED to expose the independent requested-guarantee obligation.
+
+## Receipt interpretation and remaining limits
+
+`reports/v0.2/vectors.json` records the original 30 plus these 38 cases; `reports/v0.2/mutations.json` records the 14 selected new mutants and patch identities. The final review report owns the canonical rerun after the fixture and harness corrections above. Earlier full-suite receipts with failures remain evidence of those earlier runs; a successful vector/mutation subset is not a claim that an unrelated whole-suite command passed.
+
+This document establishes no universal semantic entailment, real-world scanner accuracy, independent server execution provenance, general retry-state-machine proof, production cryptographic certification, completeness of a caller-accepted dependency basis or all-profile conformance. Exact scope compatibility is conservative equality. G27 covers one explicit exclusive interval boundary. No new continuity/ledger relation is claimed by these 38 cases; those boundaries rely on the separately retained v0.1 suite and documented interface limits.
+
+No circular product oracle was found in the literal expectation generator. Shared fixture construction utilities and the duplicated/overlapping cases above remain material limits on independence; literal expectations are not automatically correct because they are detached. The native-key subset and reason-subset assertions do not prove all unasserted fields. No unresolved implementation defect is claimed here after the explicitly recorded fixes; the final release recommendation remains conditional on the root canonical gate and independent release audit.
